Cut per-job setup on SPURS job chains. Each job thread keeps one SPU
context and clears only the local store earlier jobs on it could have
written (binary end to their highest region end, plus the context and
descriptor block) instead of zeroing a fresh 256 KB context per job;
SPURS_JOB_ZERO_LS=1 restores the full clear. spu_task_launch_check now
runs only on steps that can act: a branch to LS 0, a registered
stack-reset entry, a policy context, or with a step diagnostic enabled
(SPU_LAUNCH_CHECK_ALL=1 forces every step). Skipped steps still count.

diff --git a/runtime/spu/spu_context.h b/runtime/spu/spu_context.h
--- a/runtime/spu/spu_context.h
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_context.h
